      "side": 1,
      "message": "I added the comment.\nWhat I wanted to say is we have code to use default value to enable feature on specific release devices. (e.g. `isFeatureEnabled(..,.., isAtLeastT() /* defaultEnabled */)`) but that does not work if the devices have the flag value.\n\nSo if the flag propagate config is wrong the feature is enabled or disabled unexpectedly.\nIf we write `isAtleastT() || isFeatureEnabled()`, feature can not disabled on T+ devices by wrong flag config.",
